# Code ownership for merge-request review routing.
#
# One rule, and that is not an oversight. Every path in this repo is a pinned
# surface for at least one consumer — a lint config, a script, a role default
# and a template input all ripple the same way on a tag bump — so a per-path
# split would imply some paths are lower-stakes than others, and there is only
# one reviewer to route to either way. Add a narrower rule when a second
# maintainer exists, not before.
